proofs/`. TTL is optional (no expiry when absent), positive when supplied and at most 365 days. Verify it with `pose review run-proof <run-id> <proof-id> [--json]`. The proof signs the captured executor declaration; it is not an independent vendor receipt or human confirmation. Failed or interrupted audit records disclose their state and `complete_review=false`. Unknown or ambiguous draft decisions also keep that flag false. A true flag describes completed delivery with one draft decision, not approval or complete typed-conclusion validation. A completed run with incomplete stdin or truncated output cannot establish a completed review. Legacy runs have no captured provenance and cannot be upgraded by signing today's configuration.\n+Preview `pose review run-sign <run-id> --issuer <name> [--ttl <duration>]`, then add `--apply` to publish an immutable proof under `.pose/review-run-proofs/`. TTL is optional (no expiry when absent), positive when supplied and at most 365 days. Verify it with `pose review run-proof <run-id> <proof-id> [--json]`. The proof signs the captured executor declaration; it is not an independent vendor receipt or human confirmation. Failed or interrupted audit records disclose their state and `complete_review=false`. Unknown or ambiguous draft decisions also keep that flag false. A true flag describes completed delivery with one draft decision, not approval or complete typed-conclusion validation. A completed run with incomplete stdin or truncated output cannot establish a completed review. Legacy runs have no captured provenance and cannot be upgraded by signing today's configuration. `pose review run-proof` and the issuer lookups of the verdict readers ask the question the closeout asks: for a run whose scope is done, the proof as it was given (the record stands, the issuer still holds its pin; routine drift of the repository and the proof's expiry are not asked, because the expiry bounds when a proof may back a new attestation, not whether an attestation already given to a done scope stands); for an open scope, as the repository is now.\n \n Attach `--run <run-id> --run-proof <proof-id> --sign <issuer>` to a complete `pose review attest` request. The native issuer derives authority principal/execution bindings from the run and signs the exact reference. Criteria, tools, evidence and all ordinary preflight checks still apply. A rejecting or ambiguous draft cannot support an approval; a run-backed attestation cannot predate its completed run or signed proof. Adjudication/smoke run proofs bind their kinds but cannot be used as review attestations. Automatic validation/application of complete typed conclusions belongs to the capability, not to run signing.\n \ndiff --git a/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md b/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\nindex 3b24fdfa..3dae2548 100644\n--- a/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n+++ b/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n@@ -1057,7 +1057,7 @@ Declare executor e baseline de implementação antes do dispatch. Um bundle que\n \n Reutilize o issuer nativo e seu pin de atestações. Configure `authority_project` e `authority_audience` protegidos na policy de review; a identidade declarada do projeto deve concordar. Mantenha chaves fora do projeto. O dispatch captura origem/worktree, bundle/commit/scope/kind, configuração/argv/executável, identidades, template/body/notas do brief, stdin planejado e bytes escritos no pipe, digests de saída/transcript brutos e retidos com redação, além de completude. Escrever no pipe não prova que o fornecedor consumiu o prompt. Sessões e chaves privadas ficam fora da prova pública.\n \n-Visualize `pose review run-sign <run-id> --issuer <nome> [--ttl <duração>]` e acrescente `--apply` para publicar uma prova imutável em `.pose/review-run-proofs/`. TTL é opcional (sem expiração quando ausente), positivo quando informado e limitado a 365 dias. Verifique com `pose review run-proof <run-id> <proof-id> [--json]`. A prova assina a declaração capturada do executor; não é recibo independente do fornecedor n